## Docker / Docker Compose Rules

### Dockerfile
- Base image: `eclipse-temurin:21-jre-alpine` (not JDK in production image)
- Use Spring Boot layered JAR for faster rebuilds
- Always set `EXPOSE` to match `server.port`
- Never hardcode secrets — use environment variables

### docker-compose.yml
- Every service must have a `healthcheck` block
- Use named volumes (not bind mounts) for persistent data
- Environment variables go in `.env` file — never hardcoded in `docker-compose.yml`
- Services that depend on DB or Kafka must have `depends_on` with `condition: service_healthy`

### docker-compose.yml Health Check Template
```yaml
healthcheck:
  test: ["CMD", "wget", "--quiet", "--tries=1", "--spider", "http://localhost:8080/actuator/health"]
  interval: 30s
  timeout: 10s
  retries: 3
  start_period: 40s
```

