### Fault Tolerance Rules (all new integrations)

Every new outbound integration MUST have ALL of the following:

| Layer | Requirement | Implementation |
|-------|-------------|----------------|
| Circuit Breaker | Opens after 50% failure rate over 10 calls | `@CircuitBreaker(name=..., fallbackMethod=...)` |
| Retry | Max 3 attempts with exponential backoff | `@Retry(name=..., fallbackMethod=...)` |
| Timeout | connect 2s, read 5s | FeignClient config or WebClient timeout |
| Fallback | Returns safe default, never null | Same-signature method with Throwable param |
| Bulkhead | Isolate thread pool per downstream | `@Bulkhead(name=..., type=THREADPOOL)` |
| Observability | @Timed + CB state change logged | Auto via Micrometer + CB event listener |

**Circuit Breaker event logging (add to service config):**
```java
circuitBreakerRegistry.circuitBreaker("[name]")
    .getEventPublisher()
    .onStateTransition(e -> log.warn(
        "Circuit breaker state change. name={} from={} to={}",
        e.getCircuitBreakerName(),
        e.getStateTransition().getFromState(),
        e.getStateTransition().getToState()));
```

