## What Cascade Should Never Do
- Never implement a communication pattern not documented in the ADR
- Never write new feature code without a confirmed /architecture-review ADR
- Never block a reactive thread with a blocking JPA call — use R2DBC or boundedElastic
- Never use RestTemplate for new code — use WebClient or FeignClient
- Never expose gRPC endpoints directly to external clients — use API Gateway
- Never use GraphQL without DataLoader batching and query complexity limits
- Never new feature code reachable without a feature flag guard
- Never hardcode a flag key as a raw string — always use FeatureFlags.[CONSTANT]
- Never default a new flag to true — always false
- Never evaluate a feature flag inside a loop or @Transactional method
- Never write field-injected `@Autowired` — always constructor injection
- Never use `System.out.println` — always `@Slf4j`
- Never write Mockito in a Spock spec — use Spock `Mock()`
- Never skip the Spock spec and write implementation first
- Never write a method longer than 20 lines — extract named sub-methods
- Never use a magic number or magic string in logic — extract to a named constant or enum
- Never nest conditionals more than 2 levels — use guard clauses
- Never swallow an exception silently — always log + rethrow
- Never write a public service method without `@Timed`, entry log, and exit log
- Never log PII, passwords, tokens, or full request bodies
- Never commit if JaCoCo threshold is failing
- Never place a FeignClient or RestTemplate call inside a loop — always batch
- Never place an API call inside a @Transactional method
- Never return an unbounded List<T> from a repository without Pageable
- Never skip /code-quality before /nfr-check
- Never skip /nfr-check before /deploy-story
- Never hardcode credentials or URLs — use `application.yml` properties or env vars
